--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker `tickets/0240`. `tickets/0261` gave the registry a per-model
`input_template` because e5 needs `query: ` / `passage: ` prefixes and a harness
that ignores them under-measures e5 — it would have concluded an English model
retrieves better.

**Pooling is the same trap, one axis over, and the registry does not carry it.**
`pooling` appears zero times in `bench/models.json`. The drivers call
`extractor(batch, {pooling: 'mean'})` and zoteus hardcodes the same
(`embeddings.ts:284`), so a harness that reads the template from the registry and
then hardcodes pooling gets one axis right and the other wrong.

**Why it matters more than it looks.** Wrong pooling degrades retrieval
*silently*. It reads as the model being worse, not as a bug — so `0262`'s sweep
could reject a good candidate on it and record a confident wrong number. That is
this study's standing failure mode: a measurement that is wrong rather than
missing.

It is not uniform across models. Zotero core's own registry
(`zotero/zotero#6012`, `chrome/content/zotero/xpcom/embeddings.js`) carries
pooling per model and it varies — `cls` for the bge family, `mean` for the e5
family and all-MiniLM. So a single hardcoded value is wrong for roughly half the
field by construction.

## Relevant files

- `bench/models.json` — the registry
- `bench/registry.py` / `bench/registry.mjs` — the readers
- `bench/check_models.py` — the guard
- the drivers that call `extractor(batch, {pooling: ...})`

## Actions

1. Add a named `pooling` field with a `pooling_source` beside it, in the style of
   the existing `max_seq` / `max_seq_source` pair. Not an options bag: the
   named-field-with-provenance shape is exactly why the prefix trap was caught
   and pooling was not.
2. **Read the value off each model card. Do not infer it, and do not carry a
   value over from a sibling model because the families look alike.** Where a
   card does not state it, record that as unknown with the source saying so — an
   unknown is a finding, a guess is a defect.
3. Apply it in the drivers from the registry, alongside the input template.
4. Make the guard require the pair on every candidate record, so a new model
   cannot arrive without it.

## Artifacts produced

- `verification/probes/probe_pooling.py` — reads `1_Pooling/config.json` from each
  record's `upstream_repo`, since the ONNX mirrors publish the graph and nothing
  else. Four outcomes, never collapsed. Controls are **enforced**: it refuses to
  write an artifact if the positive control (a value attested in Zotero core) or
  the negative control comes back wrong.
- `bench/results/0421-pooling/pooling.json` — the measurement, with its controls.

## Measured, 2026-08-29

| candidate | pooling |
|---|---|
| granite-97m-multilingual-r2 | cls |
| granite-311m-multilingual-r2 | cls |
| arctic-embed-m-v2 | cls |
| gte-multilingual-base | cls |
| multilingual-e5-small | mean |
| multilingual-e5-base | mean |

Four of six are `cls`. Every transformers.js driver hardcoded `mean`.

All six also carry a `Normalize` module, recorded in the artifact. Whether the
drivers' `normalize:` flag matches per model is a second axis and is NOT settled
here — noted for `0262`.

## Test

- A record missing `pooling` or `pooling_source` fails the guard. Run it against
  the current registry first, which lacks both — a guard that cannot go red on
  today's tree is not yet a guard.
- A driver that hardcodes a pooling literal is caught, the same way a hardcoded
  model id is.

## Verification

- [ ] Every candidate record carries `pooling` and `pooling_source`
- [ ] Each value traces to its own model card, quoted in the source field
- [ ] No driver names a pooling mode; all read it from the registry
- [ ] Unknowns are recorded as unknown, never defaulted to `mean`

## Invariants

- Provenance beside every value; a value with no source is not recorded
- `0262`'s sweep should not run before this lands, or its numbers carry an
  unmeasured axis

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `pooling` + `pooling_source` on every candidate, read from cards
- [ ] Drivers resolve pooling through the registry
- [ ] Guard requires the pair; `make check` green
